.TH SI468X-PI 1 "October 2026" "si468x-pi 0.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
si468x-pi \- terminal radio application for the Silicon Labs Si468x receiver on Raspberry Pi
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B si468x-pi
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBsi468x-pi\fR is an interactive terminal and headless daemon application for controlling
the uGreen DAB Board and other Silicon Labs Si468x receiver boards on the Raspberry Pi.
It provides automatic Band III scanning, station caching, real-time DLS text display with
marquee scrolling, audio routing control (analog, I2S, or both), and hardware plugin
support (Linux evdev remotes, framebuffer displays, and HD44780 character LCDs).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
Load settings from the specified JSON \fIFILE\fR. If omitted, the standard XDG configuration
search paths are consulted (\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/si468x-pi/si468x-pi.json\fR, then \fI/etc/si468x-pi/si468x-pi.json\fR).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-spi " \fIDEV\fR"
Override the SPI character device (default: \fI/dev/spidev0.0\fR).
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-reset\-gpio " \fIN\fR"
Override the BCM GPIO pin used for hardware reset (default: \fI23\fR).
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fIdab\fR|\fIfmhd\fR"
Set tuner boot mode. Default is \fIdab\fR.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audio " \fIanalog\fR|\fIi2s\fR|\fIboth\fR"
Select audio output routing. Default is \fIanalog\fR.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-service\-id " \fIN\fR"
Tune and immediately start playing the 32-bit Service ID \fIN\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-programme " \fINAME\fR"
Play the first cached station matching \fINAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-scan
Use existing station cache; do not initiate a scan if the cache is empty.
.TP
.BR \-\-rescan
Force a fresh Band III scan even if cached stations exist.
.TP
.BR \-\-log
Enable low-level diagnostic driver logging from libsi468x.
.TP
.BR \-\-config\-example
Print a fully populated JSON configuration template to stdout and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-demo\-ui
Launch the interactive terminal UI using a synthetic source without accessing hardware.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print verbose runtime diagnostics to stderr.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Output version information and exit.

.SH INTERACTIVE CONTROLS
When run from an interactive terminal (TTY), the following keys are available:
.TP
.B Up / Down, u / d
Navigate station lists and menu choices.
.TP
.B Enter, e
Select station or menu item.
.TP
.B Menu, m, Esc, Left
Open the main menu or go back to the previous screen.
.TP
.B Home, h
Return directly to the main radio playing screen.
.TP
.B +, =
Increase volume.
.TP
.B \-
Decrease volume.
.TP
.B 0
Toggle mute.
.TP
.B q, x
Exit the application cleanly.

.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are formatted in JSON. Use \fBsi468x-pi \-\-config-example\fR to generate a starting template.
The configuration file allows customizing hardware devices, volume defaults, scan channel lists,
polling frequencies, and plugins:
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBdevice\fR: \fIspi\fR, \fIreset_gpio\fR, \fImode\fR, \fIaudio\fR, \fIregion\fR.
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBvolume\fR: \fIstart\fR (0..100 percent), \fIstep\fR (percent per step).
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBscan\fR: \fIrssi_min\fR (threshold in dBµV), \fIinclude_data\fR, \fIchannels\fR array.
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBinput\fR: array of input source definitions (stdin, evdev plugin).
.IP \[bu] 2
\fBdisplay\fR: array of display outputs (tty, fb plugin, lcd plugin).

.SH PLUGINS
Hardware drivers for input devices and displays are loaded dynamically as shared objects from
\fI/usr/local/lib/si468x-pi/\fR or next to the executable in \fIsi468x-pi-plugins/\fR:
.TP
.B si468x-pi-evdev.so
Reads Linux input event devices (\fI/dev/input/event*\fR) with configurable key mappings.
.TP
.B si468x-pi-fb.so
Renders 8x8 font text to Linux framebuffers (\fI/dev/fb*\fR) in RGB565 or XRGB8888.
.TP
.B si468x-pi-lcd.so
Drives HD44780 character LCD displays through \fI/dev/lcd\fR with automatic character set mapping.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/si468x-pi/si468x-pi.json
System-wide configuration file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.config/si468x-pi/si468x-pi.json
User configuration file.
.TP
.I $HOME/.cache/si468x-pi/cache.json
Cached station table and last played station.

